{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-daemon.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.729791Z","id":"1f22b7c5805cf9be124738cdb2b1300e9d6eb0a6c0073fdc470cf4a9452868b6","body":{"detail":"The in-daemon calibration still runs about 1.8 times slow for a whole daemon life in about 1 run in 25 under load, which lowers both ratios (a false pass only). Doubling the list's store work measured x3.61 against the list_alone_ratio budget of 3.57 (scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json:4) at its lowest, so the margin for catching a doubled list is about 1%.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":49},"end":{"line":60},"content_hash":"f10543835dfd8cd6e58b0a7ae63a3ab733a203de9d515da8c90f690f6ffabcd7"},"summary":"The gallery-alone ratio budgets have thin margins: a doubled list can pass when the calibration runs slow","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/tool-hook.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730200Z","id":"fcca66e62394aa60f8404373505f2feaf70191e5d68a743902e598978dc54753","body":{"detail":"Not taken (2026-10-01, docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-01-grok-build.md:116 (Q5)). Both harnesses can add context to any tool's result, so a hand-over there would reach the agent on its next tool call of any kind. Today the Claude Code PostToolUse hook only renews working records and prints nothing, and Grok's plugin (plugins/clax-grok/hooks/hooks.json) has no PostToolUse hook. Add it for both at once, as a tier with its own delivery and acknowledgement rules, weighing a clax hook run on every tool call.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":7},"content_hash":"9c9e415214872effcbf11a07f6c3df4e3161fecb02cc14d22ed19c6127a5dc12"},"summary":"A PostToolUse hand-over of feedback for Claude Code and Grok together","tags":["revisit:agents miss feedback that arrives mid-turn between Stop hooks","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/verify-harnesses.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730243Z","id":"2e28c034d7f0be3846a6fd1a561c4c0bd95f88de81c42e4dc5e5a338c03861a4","body":{"detail":"It checks clax init and clax uninit against the real claude, codex and pi CLIs only; grok install, list and uninstall through clax init and clax uninit are covered only by a fake Grok (crates/clax-cli/tests/grok_dedupe.rs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":214},"end":{"line":214},"content_hash":"2ddf09543d9bd433c6845c48b214dd8731f69f7d261323a3c61d818195fba4ce"},"summary":"verify-harnesses.sh does not check grok","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/ensure-clax.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730692Z","id":"66a9c4f7312187a37c758ce1c7ba5dd6132082231dbfe624cf4194ee489ed0fa","body":{"detail":"In pathological cases the wrapper spends up to PROBE_SECS (5 s) on clax --version and 5 s on clax mcp --preflight, then the shim may wait up to 5 s for a daemon start, or longer for a replacement, before it answers initialize.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":119},"end":{"line":120},"content_hash":"2a740623c3a0fe4ad69c34cd524eaf875cbf88198685aff1b33c7c6e92c5f380"},"suggested_fix":"One shared deadline for both probes, or a slow-probe line in hooks.log.","summary":"The wrapper's probes plus a daemon start can exceed Codex's MCP startup timeout","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/verify-harnesses.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730722Z","id":"30779a1b495d1bbd976efd0f1eec4ac2cbf76685140e92100a3c8699a3a922f1","body":{"detail":"Each harness's version is printed only at the top (lines 217-218); the final header repeats the build under test only. Until fixed, keep the whole output.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":444},"end":{"line":446},"content_hash":"1bd622b10b2c6834eb109890c99f491f8edc9da4782327c3dec5cc21e731fc9e"},"summary":"The harness versions are not printed above the result table, and nothing says what to paste","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/verify-harnesses.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730747Z","id":"50ccc650a7219d6f3b67b1a5c6dc1d244f537a65b795466823042239d047a960","body":{"detail":"The FAIL detail is the last line of $ROOT/seed-<harness>.log, and cleanup removes $ROOT on exit, so the rest of the log is lost.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":326},"end":{"line":336},"content_hash":"d1449e6114f99f60fe6f6f1d195610ee618ed1b96a3cdc7eca7100bf2be1047e"},"summary":"A failed seed step reports one line, and its log is deleted with the scratch root","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/verify-harnesses.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730772Z","id":"c22e973765b3c9637692aaf9ba4ca88cd5fffa4b23fa82b574cddef417f6321f","body":{"detail":"setpgrp runs in the child after fork; a signal in the microseconds before it can make $stop signal a process group that does not exist yet and wait for the command.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":123},"end":{"line":124},"content_hash":"da31bc255bc77c6b1b2df93e59e1c46fab8d16544729d3239a4ab96183d10db8"},"suggested_fix":"Also call setpgid($pid, $pid) in the parent after fork.","summary":"The watchdog sets the process group only in the child","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/verify-harnesses.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730798Z","id":"dab8712cf425c8573e2e00fd01470933774cb95ffaa8ef5bd355d3fc599dbb22","body":{"detail":"Each command runs in a process group of its own (setpgrp), which is a background group on the terminal; a harness that opens /dev/tty and reads it is stopped, then killed at VERIFY_TIMEOUT and reported as '(timeout after Ns)'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":109},"end":{"line":131},"content_hash":"cc2e6947a401a85dbb7f6f7892c63de0b1b9019bf86ffa67ffade2712bc4920f"},"summary":"A CLI that reads /dev/tty is stopped by SIGTTIN and reported as a timeout","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/verify-harnesses.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730822Z","id":"0606ce6d916b7b8cf375d052b4956752a58816a476093c30ad135507d4ff0559","body":{"detail":"The watchdog signals the command's process group (kill -$pid); a descendant that started a session of its own is outside it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":20},"content_hash":"693898f64bf9f5fa20c7664b48e585faf7c4e6563ac7e3b95c1a5473968f9c5b"},"suggested_fix":"Say 'with its process group'.","summary":"The header says each command is killed 'with everything it started'; a descendant that calls setsid survives","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/verify-harnesses.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730846Z","id":"692aeb40f56b1424db2f248656efc4a03758e7b9aaa37d99b97a4c6df55c717b","body":{"detail":"Only the header's '(from CLAX_BIN)' says the build under test was not built from this checkout; an exported CLAX_BIN from an older build is easy to miss.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":91},"end":{"line":93},"content_hash":"54d60d9a570bde1aef3e267ef7237038e9827999e25d2f9d54c4b4c5090f5491"},"summary":"An exported CLAX_BIN skips the build with no note beyond the header","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/verify-harnesses.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730869Z","id":"9e509c370beeaa384e02b46390e9425a59112561a478fef1dcbb536f096944e1","body":{"detail":"The INT trap exits 130, which runs cleanup; a second INT while cleanup runs (clax stop can take up to 30 s) interrupts it before rm -rf $ROOT.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":142},"end":{"line":151},"content_hash":"ccdc06724d484636423060bb20ac00cb5c470d084ce3414e0fd9d4b1709004f8"},"suggested_fix":"Ignore INT, TERM and HUP at the top of cleanup.","summary":"A second Ctrl-C during cleanup can leave the scratch root behind","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-daemon.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730913Z","id":"0e2a613c3ef1c9aba31ede4949eb53dd6451ecdc786b6fd67212f9d846807dda","body":{"detail":"It does not run the loads together, does not cover several viewers, asset uploads, MCP wait_for_feedback, the sweepers or clax doctor (none of which stalled cheap requests when measured by hand). Besides the gallery and inbox requests alone (lines 27-33), it judges no request slower than its probes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":6},"end":{"line":18},"content_hash":"5d2d22f2f0eea2a5c8a14ecedf8b50e5c2eaa8caed3eaf0314086df378ae0e8f"},"summary":"The daemon latency gate runs its loads one at a time, for one viewer, on loopback","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-clients.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731023Z","id":"511203ef3828552d8596dbf1f8fcaaf9b0fe15ff6585b5b371ca84b1f87d4940","body":{"detail":"Its clients run on the daemon's own machine over loopback from one source address, so near 16,000 clients it runs out of client ports, not daemon limits. Tabs sharing one stream through the shared worker are checked only by web/e2e/streams.spec.ts:176 (thirty tabs, the daemon's own count of open streams through /api/_test/stream/open in debug builds).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":10},"end":{"line":14},"content_hash":"520c4a43b992eb12dfb97c0f34efe5934f51495d9e2fe427238850732ca2951c"},"summary":"The realtime load gate drives raw /api/stream sockets from one source address: it stops near 16,000 clients and never measures real tabs","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731810Z","id":"39562e1125375035c0a8ea3214e707f7ee268df5e36d450a5c361549026fe126","body":{"detail":"They run first, alone, because several were timing-sensitive. Since 508ebe9 the view-mounting and child-process tests run under limits that end hangs only (MOUNT_TIMEOUT_MS 30 s, CHILD_TIMEOUT_MS 60 s, web/shell/src/test/timeouts.ts), so moving them into the lanes would save about 9 s of a gates run.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":141},"end":{"line":147},"content_hash":"43ba07359a2927073b8825eff55b3404c52ce0a02a6b7953d444a1c18c2256c6"},"summary":"The shell's unit tests run alone (about 9 s); they may now join the lanes","tags":["gate-speed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731837Z","id":"a91e1d1bdfcaac139c71257ee71ac087f2d74011a97b4d729f965554fd2a57d5","body":{"detail":"The daemon gate also keeps its three rounds, so one noisy round cannot fail it. A smaller seed would hide cost that grows with the home: with the attention queries' planner hints removed, the quick daemon latency gate failed 'attention alone' at about 460 ms against its 50 ms limit.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":26},"end":{"line":28},"content_hash":"4a494227b0e5c3ca7450b24ea7d6bd0f951d0a2ea41b6b9714dee613e560d3da"},"summary":"The quick perf gates keep the full seed and client count and shorten only their windows","tags":["gate-speed","perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-clients.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:26:52.183601Z","id":"2fae41b92c5d2a7666d11c3a6fb18f6e96b7466d6d9f7db468f0e8e22cfe2922","body":{"detail":"The measure is the median, over slow_rounds floods of flood_batches document batches, of the daemon's footprint growth (budget 1024 KB). Measured medians were 0-32 KB per flood with and without CPU load, against 320-448 KB for the earlier single-flood RSS measure. A build that keeps a slow client's whole backlog (QUEUE in crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs raised from 64 to 1<<20) was built but never measured: its first run stalled in macOS's assessment of new executables. That a kept backlog exceeds the budget is inferred from its size (5000 events with 160-character paths per flood), not observed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":810},"end":{"line":820},"content_hash":"be67e806b167263d6cedfacadd444a8750ddaa218457c63c4f32d442b666ac9e"},"suggested_fix":"Run scripts/perf-clients.py --quick once against that variant binary and confirm slow_growth_kb fails.","summary":"slow_growth_kb has not been shown to catch a kept backlog","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-daemon.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:29:45.207732Z","id":"6c59de7834f6342fa8cea21d86457e02089e95835e873804529cfb7b38497762","body":{"detail":"The in-daemon calibration still runs about 1.8 times slow for a whole daemon life in about 1 run in 25 under load, which lowers both ratios (a false pass only). Doubling the list's store work measured x3.61 against the list_alone_ratio budget of 3.57 (scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json:4) at its lowest, so the margin for catching a doubled list is about 1%.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":63},"content_hash":"f10543835dfd8cd6e58b0a7ae63a3ab733a203de9d515da8c90f690f6ffabcd7"},"summary":"The gallery-alone ratio budgets have thin margins: a doubled list can pass when the calibration runs slow","supersedes":"1f22b7c5805cf9be124738cdb2b1300e9d6eb0a6c0073fdc470cf4a9452868b6","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:29:45.207808Z","id":"19255113137d10b3ec2426bd4233ed8515c37d894f55a75fa094ee7878c6b4ea","body":{"detail":"The daemon gate also keeps its three rounds, so one noisy round cannot fail it. A smaller seed would hide cost that grows with the home: with the attention queries' planner hints removed, the quick daemon latency gate failed 'attention alone' at about 460 ms against its 50 ms limit.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":29},"end":{"line":32},"content_hash":"5701966e2364a33cdeb762e65feaf5605f41e7f10732c2cb49d41601ee27c9ef"},"summary":"The quick perf gates keep the full seed and client count and shorten only their windows","supersedes":"a91e1d1bdfcaac139c71257ee71ac087f2d74011a97b4d729f965554fd2a57d5","tags":["gate-speed","perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/test-release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:54:19.636160Z","id":"e44d2cd74c4e96be3a2e13b1284523ff76d7783b899b0129575b2d33b26b47dc","body":{"detail":"Failure: scripts/test-release.sh copies FILES into a scratch tree and runs scripts/sync-skill-tools.py there; since 7757145 sync-skill-tools.py:52 also reads docs/usage.md, which is not in FILES, so the check raises FileNotFoundError and the test reports 'FAIL: bump-version writes every version'. The 'release scripts' lane of scripts/quality_gates.sh fails on main for this reason (reproduced alone: scripts/test-release.sh exits 1).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":22},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"e544bc4d5f39b28af30a329c6b14be1d55e98547f2a1a7da0ebd72e285fa0d36"},"suggested_fix":"Add docs/usage.md to FILES in scripts/test-release.sh.","summary":"The release script test's file list lacks docs/usage.md, so bump-version fails in its scratch copy","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/test-release.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:57:55.148047Z","id":"51cb1cf2b2014b98b6dcec05af17ad9f6ef974f5b5aee10b6d2a6bde5af1e3d6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:8fa97f3","summary":"scripts/test-release.sh now copies docs/usage.md; bash scripts/test-release.sh exits 0 ('release script tests passed').","supersedes":"e44d2cd74c4e96be3a2e13b1284523ff76d7783b899b0129575b2d33b26b47dc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/ensure-clax.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.621302Z","id":"1b7bcfd2f613be332e31d839a4aa1df3f317380adb9f9ea1892de959bddafa29","body":{"detail":"In pathological cases the wrapper spends up to PROBE_SECS (5 s) on clax --version and 5 s on clax mcp --preflight, then the shim may wait up to 5 s for a daemon start, or longer for a replacement, before it answers initialize.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":142},"end":{"line":143},"content_hash":"2a740623c3a0fe4ad69c34cd524eaf875cbf88198685aff1b33c7c6e92c5f380"},"suggested_fix":"One shared deadline for both probes, or a slow-probe line in hooks.log.","summary":"The wrapper's probes plus a daemon start can exceed Codex's MCP startup timeout","supersedes":"66a9c4f7312187a37c758ce1c7ba5dd6132082231dbfe624cf4194ee489ed0fa","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:13:05.505970Z","id":"d1a5ca64cd45fed129eb67bccc73011dfc748184cabbd79aa46483684f33bd42","body":{"detail":"They run first, alone, because several were timing-sensitive. Since 508ebe9 the view-mounting and child-process tests run under limits that end hangs only (MOUNT_TIMEOUT_MS 30 s, CHILD_TIMEOUT_MS 60 s, web/shell/src/test/timeouts.ts), so moving them into the lanes would save about 9 s of a gates run.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":153},"end":{"line":160},"content_hash":"6115d495e619e1d116c1414158a591fcebd9d0f284301f6a25e22ad6a444938d"},"summary":"The shell's unit tests run alone (about 9 s); they may now join the lanes","supersedes":"39562e1125375035c0a8ea3214e707f7ee268df5e36d450a5c361549026fe126","tags":["gate-speed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-wasm.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:40:09.187588Z","id":"eb01cab47569cb291eda737f74295e4e78c8edb6b0c05898501916ffb058f165","body":{"detail":"scripts/quality_gates.sh has no lane running scripts/check-wasm.sh, and .github/workflows/ci.yml (ubuntu-latest) installs neither the wasm32-unknown-unknown rustup target nor a known wasm-capable clang, so a change that breaks `cargo check -p clax-core --target wasm32-unknown-unknown` (a new std::os::unix use, a tokio feature that pulls mio) passes every gate. Only `just check-wasm` runs it, by hand.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":10},"content_hash":"12014541790fcdeb02c1ff3ff3f12e3fbb64faf74b536688d527a9c378ba9fee"},"suggested_fix":"Add a gate in lane_lint that runs scripts/check-wasm.sh, and in ci.yml add the wasm32-unknown-unknown target and an LLVM with a wasm32 backend (Ubuntu's clang has one; set LLVM_BIN if llvm-ar is versioned).","summary":"The wasm32 check of clax-core runs in no gate and no CI job","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-wasm.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:18:31.974104Z","id":"d2d39ab3340365e3cfd52257d7d3b610bdd668c9f3d40426004ab59a41162f93","body":{"detail":"`cargo clippy --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p clax-core -- -D warnings` (with CC/AR from Homebrew LLVM) fails with drop_non_drop at crates/clax-core/src/gitctx.rs:895 (`drop(stdout)`, ChildStdout has no Drop on that target). scripts/check-wasm.sh runs `cargo check`, which passes. Also, getrandom 0.3.4 (Cargo.lock) picks its wasm_js backend from the feature alone: the check passes with RUSTFLAGS overriding .cargo/config.toml's `--cfg getrandom_backend=\"wasm_js\"`.","kind":"comment","references":"eb01cab47569cb291eda737f74295e4e78c8edb6b0c05898501916ffb058f165","summary":"clippy -D warnings for wasm32 fails today, so a gate cannot just run clippy there","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:25:07.090642Z","id":"cad9aae716290b5e1140ab9757bc3d2ca441d873c553eee4c47fcb054a60dff1","body":{"detail":"They run first, alone, because several were timing-sensitive. Since 508ebe9 the view-mounting and child-process tests run under limits that end hangs only (MOUNT_TIMEOUT_MS 30 s, CHILD_TIMEOUT_MS 60 s, web/shell/src/test/timeouts.ts), so moving them into the lanes would save about 9 s of a gates run.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":166},"end":{"line":173},"content_hash":"44ee65e637faf9d26b4cbed0ca05ad97f8fac588dad028418a1ea11356c4e110"},"summary":"The shell's unit tests run alone (about 9 s); they may now join the lanes","supersedes":"d1a5ca64cd45fed129eb67bccc73011dfc748184cabbd79aa46483684f33bd42","tags":["gate-speed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-wasm.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:49:19.123197Z","id":"f7a7babd97c31991fc6c0cffaff7a09bd20a7883e38d1a84d0622e6c162e102d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"eb01cab47569cb291eda737f74295e4e78c8edb6b0c05898501916ffb058f165","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":10},"content_hash":"229f243767342448a9948a6f2365c61a3554be145fdd44678219a33c4628aeaa"},"summary":"The check now covers clax-core, clax-rt, clax-mcp and clax-server by default (scripts/check-wasm.sh with no arguments); it still runs in no gate","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-wasm.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:17:05.481156Z","id":"67621526aeaf0c0f7a8b38d33e21f39977769240e353e1471c7cd7b08e030118","body":{"detail":"scripts/quality_gates.sh has no lane running scripts/check-wasm.sh (which with no arguments checks clax-core, clax-rt, clax-mcp and clax-server for wasm32-unknown-unknown, warnings denied), and .github/workflows/ci.yml (ubuntu-latest) installs neither the wasm32-unknown-unknown rustup target nor a known wasm-capable clang, so a change that breaks the wasm32 build of any of them (a new std::os::unix use, a tokio feature that pulls mio, a non-Send field in AppState) passes every gate. Only `just check-wasm` runs it, by hand.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":10},"content_hash":"229f243767342448a9948a6f2365c61a3554be145fdd44678219a33c4628aeaa"},"suggested_fix":"Add a gate in lane_lint that runs scripts/check-wasm.sh, and in ci.yml add the wasm32-unknown-unknown target and an LLVM with a wasm32 backend (Ubuntu's clang has one; set LLVM_BIN if llvm-ar is versioned).","summary":"The wasm32 check of clax-core, clax-rt, clax-mcp and clax-server runs in no gate and no CI job","supersedes":"eb01cab47569cb291eda737f74295e4e78c8edb6b0c05898501916ffb058f165","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-wasm.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:12:06.160929Z","id":"66e95d2ea22782cbc37390be298fd766ce5ef445f0e65031e13510713967d590","body":{"detail":".github/workflows/ci.yml and rust-toolchain.toml add the wasm32-unknown-unknown target, and the script now also tries Debian and Ubuntu's /usr/lib/llvm-<N>/bin. Whether ubuntu-latest has a clang there that targets wasm32 beside an llvm-ar was not checked; the first CI run of the gates shows it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":29},"end":{"line":41},"content_hash":"e66b7d02889242a086cff19ef6e715715aeb07f55cc86dd9f77faecf1ca7e1c7"},"summary":"The wasm32 lane has run on macOS only: CI's Ubuntu LLVM is unverified","tags":["gates","ci","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-wasm.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:22:55.244729Z","id":"cc73bc73ef882290fc0bb205fe711601ff240333e95e4015f1887bac77148e6a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:28ad843c","summary":"Fixed: scripts/quality_gates.sh runs scripts/check-wasm.sh (clax-core, clax-rt, clax-mcp, clax-server) in its own wasm lane, which fails naming a missing LLVM or rustup target; ci.yml and rust-toolchain.toml add the wasm32-unknown-unknown target. scripts/quality_gates.sh at 28ad843c printed 'wasm32 check  ok  61.4s'. Whether CI's Ubuntu LLVM is found is open in 66e95d2e.","supersedes":"eb01cab47569cb291eda737f74295e4e78c8edb6b0c05898501916ffb058f165","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:23:33.186318Z","id":"3042ce81872845c5752e79c9830d948f190a9b3754190b81f8da227cd6d0bf17","body":{"detail":"They run first, alone, because several were timing-sensitive. Since 508ebe9 the view-mounting and child-process tests run under limits that end hangs only (MOUNT_TIMEOUT_MS 30 s, CHILD_TIMEOUT_MS 60 s, web/shell/src/test/timeouts.ts), so moving them into the lanes would save about 9 s of a gates run.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":159},"end":{"line":166},"content_hash":"6115d495e619e1d116c1414158a591fcebd9d0f284301f6a25e22ad6a444938d"},"summary":"The shell's unit tests run alone (about 9 s); they may now join the lanes","supersedes":"d1a5ca64cd45fed129eb67bccc73011dfc748184cabbd79aa46483684f33bd42","tags":["gate-speed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/smoke-comment-loop.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:24:06.500356Z","id":"a22f9051e982ea41982304860f0d4e9e3e54114cf28b4242814e364f9789b4ed","body":{"detail":"scripts/smoke-comment-loop.sh fails with 'smoke: FAIL: payload format' on 89ae21af and on rust-server-wasm alike (run alone with CLAX_TEST_BIN set): line 5 of the payload is 'Viewer (not connected): \"Make this a two-column layout and drop the third bullet.\"'. The browser thread's viewer is never claimed for the owner, and Connected::is_unconnected (crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs) marks unattributed authors as decided in that file's records. akesling/clax-artifacts' copy of the script expects 'Viewer:' too.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":175},"end":{"line":177},"content_hash":"a1816e73b48f4eecd077733b86716a70aa218bdbd4a9c173e68da65bf3efee7f"},"suggested_fix":"Expect 'Viewer (not connected):' (or make the smoke's browser a claimed owner identity, if the payload should read as the owner's).","summary":"The comment-loop smoke expects 'Viewer:' where the feedback payload now reads 'Viewer (not connected):', so the gate fails","tags":["gates","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:00:52.651097Z","id":"3265e6fb2c4ff164f27898147a8c85f8efd4a143a7938e784e1595d450e6be5f","body":{"detail":"They run first, alone, because several were timing-sensitive. Since 508ebe9 the view-mounting and child-process tests run under limits that end hangs only (MOUNT_TIMEOUT_MS 30 s, CHILD_TIMEOUT_MS 60 s, web/shell/src/test/timeouts.ts), so moving them into the lanes would save about 9 s of a gates run.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":171},"end":{"line":178},"content_hash":"6115d495e619e1d116c1414158a591fcebd9d0f284301f6a25e22ad6a444938d"},"summary":"The shell's unit tests run alone (about 9 s); they may now join the lanes","supersedes":"3042ce81872845c5752e79c9830d948f190a9b3754190b81f8da227cd6d0bf17","tags":["gate-speed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:19.063044Z","id":"5dfbf30acf42c034ed72a27c4c468fc3a8a749b50084ca1afd15389944d352b1","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of 3265e6fb2c4ff164f27898147a8c85f8efd4a143a7938e784e1595d450e6be5f, the other head of the same record; that one stays at scripts/quality_gates.sh:171:178.","supersedes":"cad9aae716290b5e1140ab9757bc3d2ca441d873c553eee4c47fcb054a60dff1","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
